# A write pin of a List element or a struct member that is a handle or a box (`x: &xs[i]` of a
# Decimal, a String, an enum with payloads, an Int?, `&people[0].name`) writes the element in
# place: an assignment or compound update through the pin drops the old value and stores the new
# one where it lives. A struct element's pin writes its fields in place. Repeated rewrites leave
# the heap intact at every optimization level.
fixture: write_pins_of_handle_elements_write_in_place/input
